{
  "case_id": "2012-11-10189",
  "document_hash": "0eedf2219cbdf1f2bc7cc94c98dad9a49a9852f6a2794414539ba66bcf2b3727",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2012-11-10189",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0eedf2219cbdf1f2bc7cc94c98dad9a49a9852f6a2794414539ba66bcf2b3727",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0eedf2219cbd-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We will hear next this morning in Case 11-10189, Trevino v. Thaler."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Warren A. Wolf",
      "case_id": "2012-11-10189",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0eedf2219cbdf1f2bc7cc94c98dad9a49a9852f6a2794414539ba66bcf2b3727",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0eedf2219cbd-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Texas Court of Criminal Appeals has said, repeatedly, \"As a general rule, a defendant should not raise an issue of ineffective assistance of counsel on direct appeal,\" and has recognized that Texas procedure make it, \"virtually impossible for appellate counsel to adequately present such a claim.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2012-11-10189",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0eedf2219cbdf1f2bc7cc94c98dad9a49a9852f6a2794414539ba66bcf2b3727",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0eedf2219cbd-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Suppose the State's position were not as you accurately have stated the Texas Court of Criminal Appeal. It didn't say collateral review is the preferred route. It said either way will do. You can bring it up on direct appeal, or you can bring it up on collateral."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Warren A. Wolf",
      "case_id": "2012-11-10189",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0eedf2219cbdf1f2bc7cc94c98dad9a49a9852f6a2794414539ba66bcf2b3727",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0eedf2219cbd-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, there's two -- actually, Texas has a dual-track system. It was developed in 1995, a year before the Federal system was developed in AEDPA. And the concept -- and the reason for it -- the rationale, was to expedite these type of claims, especially in death penalty claims, under Section 11.071."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2012-11-10189",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0eedf2219cbdf1f2bc7cc94c98dad9a49a9852f6a2794414539ba66bcf2b3727",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0eedf2219cbd-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Could you give us, in a sentence or two, the test that you would like us to apply? Where a State does not, like Arizona, prohibit the raising of this issue on direct appeal, Martinez, nevertheless, applies where the State does blank. Fill in the blank."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Warren A. Wolf",
      "case_id": "2012-11-10189",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0eedf2219cbdf1f2bc7cc94c98dad9a49a9852f6a2794414539ba66bcf2b3727",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0eedf2219cbd-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Okay. I would suggest the rule to be that Martinez applies when a State channels ineffective assistance of counsel claims to State habeas and makes it impracticable in the vast majority of cases to raise the claim on direct appeal."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2012-11-10189",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0eedf2219cbdf1f2bc7cc94c98dad9a49a9852f6a2794414539ba66bcf2b3727",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0eedf2219cbd-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Why is it a second bite when the Texas Supreme Court -- court of criminal appeals, has said, again and again, as a general rule, defendants should not raise ineffective assistance of trial counsel on direct appeal, should raise it on collateral review?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2012-11-10189",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0eedf2219cbdf1f2bc7cc94c98dad9a49a9852f6a2794414539ba66bcf2b3727",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0eedf2219cbd-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: I don't -- does the statement \"defendants should not raise ineffective assistance of trial counsel on direct appeal\" doesn't mean what it says?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2012-11-10189",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0eedf2219cbdf1f2bc7cc94c98dad9a49a9852f6a2794414539ba66bcf2b3727",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0eedf2219cbd-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: But then -- but the comment is that the record has to be done within a very short period of time, and the -- and the trial record isn't even available for -- the transcript, for some 7 months."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2012-11-10189",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0eedf2219cbdf1f2bc7cc94c98dad9a49a9852f6a2794414539ba66bcf2b3727",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0eedf2219cbd-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: That -- that has never happened in the State of Texas in a capital case, I take it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Oldham",
      "case_id": "2012-11-10189",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0eedf2219cbdf1f2bc7cc94c98dad9a49a9852f6a2794414539ba66bcf2b3727",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0eedf2219cbd-0001-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. OLDHAM: I'm not aware of a capital case, but it has been done in many, many noncapital cases. And the Court of Criminal Appeals has specifically blessed it, especially -- particularly in a case involving a Wiggins type ineffective assistance of counsel at punishment phase. That is a case called Cooks v. State. It's cited on pages 32 and 34 of our brief."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2012-11-10189",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0eedf2219cbdf1f2bc7cc94c98dad9a49a9852f6a2794414539ba66bcf2b3727",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0eedf2219cbd-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: So what do you do with the 75-day rule, which I think is absolute, which says, if the court hasn't ruled on the new trial within 75 days, the matter ends?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2012-11-10189",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0eedf2219cbdf1f2bc7cc94c98dad9a49a9852f6a2794414539ba66bcf2b3727",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0eedf2219cbd-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: So he can do this -- I didn't understand this. I'm sorry. Joe Smith is convicted on day 1. The transcript appears 9 months later. Okay? 9 months later his new lawyer, who is supposed to proceed on appeal, reads the transcript. He thinks, hmm, I think there was a problem with his lawyer at the trial, and I would like to raise this claim and get a new trial. And you are saying what he does is he goes back to the trial court, and he says, Judge, I just read this, it raises some factual matters; will you please give me an evidentiary hearing with the old lawyer there and me there, so we can develop this? Now, that is what -- how Texas works?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2012-11-10189",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0eedf2219cbdf1f2bc7cc94c98dad9a49a9852f6a2794414539ba66bcf2b3727",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0eedf2219cbd-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Is it true that it's the county that reimburses the direct appeal counsel and the State reimburses the habeas counsel?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2012-11-10189",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0eedf2219cbdf1f2bc7cc94c98dad9a49a9852f6a2794414539ba66bcf2b3727",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0eedf2219cbd-0001-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: There's clearly no Martinez protection. The question you are being asked, I think, boils down to whether we should develop a new case, Martinez plus, in which -- even though there is, technically, the ability to raise it, which is all that Martinez spoke about, the mere fact that the ability to raise it is not effective enough should produce the same result that Martinez produced."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2012-11-10189",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0eedf2219cbdf1f2bc7cc94c98dad9a49a9852f6a2794414539ba66bcf2b3727",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0eedf2219cbd-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: What happens -- imagine we have a State supreme court, and it says, okay, you could raise this claim on appeal, we don't advise it, we think -- it's so much easier to do it in State habeas. Please do it in State habeas. It's not absolutely binding, but do it. Okay? That's what they are saying."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Oldham",
      "case_id": "2012-11-10189",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0eedf2219cbdf1f2bc7cc94c98dad9a49a9852f6a2794414539ba66bcf2b3727",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0eedf2219cbd-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. OLDHAM: We believe that Martinez applies where it said that it applies, and that is where a State makes a deliberate choice to disallow all claims on direct appeal."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2012-11-10189",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0eedf2219cbdf1f2bc7cc94c98dad9a49a9852f6a2794414539ba66bcf2b3727",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0eedf2219cbd-0002-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the 1989 American Bar Association guideline, 11.9.2, which specifically told the direct appeal lawyer in this case to raise every colorable claim he could, regardless of any State procedures to the contrary."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2012-11-10189",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0eedf2219cbdf1f2bc7cc94c98dad9a49a9852f6a2794414539ba66bcf2b3727",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0eedf2219cbd-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Has there ever been such a case, any case in which a direct appeal counsel has been held ineffective for failing to present a Wiggins claim?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Wolf)",
      "case_id": "2012-11-10189",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0eedf2219cbdf1f2bc7cc94c98dad9a49a9852f6a2794414539ba66bcf2b3727",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0eedf2219cbd-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. WOLF: I want to be very clear about this abatement issue. The abatement issue, as Justice Alito just said, is only available -- as referred in our brief on page 6, is only available when there is a denial of the constitutional right to an attorney."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2012-11-10189",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0eedf2219cbdf1f2bc7cc94c98dad9a49a9852f6a2794414539ba66bcf2b3727",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0eedf2219cbd-0002-0007",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Texas scheme, because of that abuse of the writ, proceeds -- causes procedural default, and that puts us in this quandary, where a person like Mr. Trevino is unable to get relief because he has an ineffective trial lawyer."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2012-11-10189",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "0eedf2219cbdf1f2bc7cc94c98dad9a49a9852f6a2794414539ba66bcf2b3727",
      "evidence_id": "unavailable-0eedf2219cbd-55",
      "kind": "fact",
